# Open in Rider or Visual Studio and run the requests one by one. Watch X-Elapsed-Ms in each response.
@host = http://localhost:5080

### 1. The first call queries the "database" (about 300 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 2. The same call again comes from the cache (about 1 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 3. A cached list
GET {{host}}/products?category=keyboards

### 4. Change a price: invalidates product 1 and the lists, nothing else
PUT {{host}}/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 119 }

### 5. Product 1 is loaded again, with the new price
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 6. Product 2 is still cached
GET {{host}}/products/2

### 7. Hits, misses and entries
GET {{host}}/methodcache/stats

### 8. What is cached right now
GET {{host}}/methodcache/entries

### 9. Every cached method's policy and where each value came from
GET {{host}}/methodcache/methods

### 10. Invalidate by tag from the outside
POST {{host}}/methodcache/invalidate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tags": ["products"] }

### 11. Health check
GET {{host}}/health
